'''The Mandalorian's IB-94 blaster pistol''', also referred to as '''Mando's blaster''',<ref name="DB">{{Databank|mando-s-blaster|Mando's blaster}}</ref> was an [[IB-94 blaster]] pistol manufactured by [[BlasTech Industries]] that the [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] carried with him during his [[bounty]] hunting career.

==Description==
Djarin's [[blaster pistol]] was a rare model with impressive range and firepower.<ref name="DB" />

==History==
[[File:DinDjarin-TMH.png|thumb|left|200px|The Mandalorian Din Djarin holding his IB-94]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date Note">{{MandoDate|1}}</ref> [[Din Djarin]] used this [[blaster]] in various missions in the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]. While on the [[Water|ice]] [[planet]] [[Pagodon]], he used the weapon while fending off a group of trawlers at a [[Boatman's Reach|public house]], shooting the controls to the door that sliced [[Quarren Trawler|one of them]] in half. During his [[Mission to Arvala-7|mission]] to retrieve [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] on [[Arvala-7]], he used the weapon in a shootout with [[Unidentified Nikto mercenary gang|Nikto mercenaries]] alongside fellow [[bounty hunter]] [[droid]] [[IG-11]], and later shot the droid when he attempted to kill Grogu.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

Upon delivering Grogu to an [[Imperial Remnant safe house]] on [[Nevarro]], the Mandalorian had a change of heart and [[Incident on Nevarro|rescued Grogu]] from the facility; using the blaster to kill a number of [[stormtrooper]]s in the process. He later used it against members of the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]], who had ambushed him as he attempted to escape the [[planet]].<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> While infiltrating a [[Klatooinian raiders|Klatooinian tribe's]] [[Klatooinian wikiup|outpost]] with [[Carasynthia Dune]] on [[Sorgan]], the Mandalorian used the blaster to create a makeshift exit within their camp as they escaped. After giving his [[Amban phase-pulse blaster]] to Dune, he used the blaster to fend off the Klatooinians while [[Skirmish on Sorgan|defending]] a [[Unidentified human tribe|human tribe's]] [[Unidentified village (Sorgan)|village]].<ref name="Chapter 4">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 4: Sanctuary}}</ref> Upon arriving on [[Tatooine]], he used the blaster to scare a group of [[DUM-series pit droid|pit droids]] when they attempted to repair his [[starship]]. He later used the weapon to kill his former partner [[Toro Calican]] after the latter had betrayed him following their [[Hunt for Fennec Shand|previous mission]].<ref name="Chapter 5">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 5: The Gunslinger}}</ref>

[[File:Mando-blaster-databank.png|thumb|right|250px|Din Djarin wields his IB-94 before the Battle for Mos Espa]]
While working with a team of [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] to rescue a [[prisoner]] in the [[Bothan-Five incident|''Bothan-Five'' incident]], the Mandalorian used the blaster to deal with a number of [[New Republic]] [[N5 sentry droid|security droids]] on a [[New Republic Correctional Transport]]. After his team betrayed and tossed him into a [[prison]], he attempted to fire the weapon at them, but the bolt bounced off the door and around the prison, hitting him instead. After the Mandalorian escaped, he used the weapon during a scuffle with [[Burg]], failing to hit him as the [[Devaronian]] knocked his arm away.<ref name="Chapter 6" /> Din later used his pistol on [[Tython]] when he tried to protect Grogu.<ref name="Chapter 14">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 14: The Tragedy}}</ref> Djarin later wielded his IB-94 in the [[Battle of Mos Espa|Battle for Mos Espa]] when he fought alongside [[Daimyo]] [[Boba Fett]].<ref name="BOBF Chapter 7">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>

{{Weapon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The blaster pistol first appeared in [[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian|Chapter 1]] of the [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 1" /> which aired on [[November 12]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref> It was first identified by its entry in the [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]].<ref name="DB" /> Its design is based upon the [https://www.forgottenweapons.com/early-automatic-pistols/bergmann-no1-1894 Bergmann 1894 No. 1] semi-automatic pistol, albeit with some modifications.<ref name="ForgotWeapon">{{YouTube|video=JvGa2c3rEuE|text=The Mandalorian Carries an 1894 Bergmann No.1|channel=channel/UCrfKGpvbEQXcbe68dzXgJuA|name=Forgotten Weapons}}</ref>

